[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186054719 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-29930a9c-51d8-56d8-87b6-15535f5105d7" "question-5237ac2b-249d-5de5-a0f0-312a03200ea8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-29930a9c-51d8-56d8-87b6-15535f5105d7" :question/id #uuid "29930a9c-51d8-56d8-87b6-15535f5105d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124392" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e597e317f32a2a9a3757ce583a2b053f4cba1da1a2119c572671e7edc96c61e4.png)\n\nThe point $P(\\frac{6}{7},\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7})$ lies on the unit circle, as shown. What is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/fb/fb0da765a857607ce0c8f13690efaa2f0d504ccaa51899a23044ee4ed17f0aa5.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=\\frac{6}{7}$ and $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{6}{7},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7}.\n$$\n\nKnowing that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we can calculate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7})}{(\\frac{6}{7})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-82c3804a-ba42-5eda-8d70-9caba3ae75d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-82c3804a-ba42-5eda-8d70-9caba3ae75d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "82c3804a-ba42-5eda-8d70-9caba3ae75d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-05b0de47-6d93-56f4-9eec-48894f36d56e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3a4fe516-3675-584c-b3d4-a4182956369b" "answer-72ba0ba6-9d3d-570e-859e-0393addd7b86" "answer-f948c330-b81c-5ef2-94de-f3c68097c2a2" "answer-05b0de47-6d93-56f4-9eec-4889